cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use VIGIL in research, please cite this repository."
title: "VIGIL: An Autonomous Art Machine for Reading the World"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sannikov
    given-names: Eugene
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-9917-8461"
repository-code: "https://github.com/esannikov/VIGIL"
url: "https://github.com/esannikov/VIGIL"
version: "0.1.0-research-preview"
date-released: "2026-08-05"
abstract: >-
  VIGIL is a trace-governed autonomous art machine that reads public world
  signals, develops five visual positions, generates images, critiques the
  resulting pixels, selects one work before human feedback, and learns through
  artifact-bound review and controlled memory.
keywords:
  - computational creativity
  - autonomous art
  - generative AI
  - visual metaphor
  - agent memory
  - AI in art
